as founded in 2016 and is headquartered in Willow Park, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew D. Wilks | President, CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 42 | Compensation: $564,589 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $852K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, declining at 7%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["ProFrac Holding Corp. is a small-cap energy business with a $547M market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -9.5pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -3% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $20M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -21.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 15.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 84% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -9.5pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 27% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 47% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4650958583345528},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $9.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a s